# Single page notification button

Name the event and the channel, and change the displayed state only when the responsible service confirms it. Someone who subscribes to updates about a page must be able to stop from the same place.

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation. They do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

For household notifications, route to a real automation or notification preference that Home Assistant owns. Name the event and destination, such as an existing mobile notification channel. Documentation release alerts can link to a repository subscription, with the external account context stated.

## Structure and behaviour

Keep loading, subscribed, unsubscribed and failed states distinct. Failure leaves the earlier confirmed state in place. A bell icon is decorative when visible text names the action.

## Home Assistant boundary

This theme adds no email subscription backend and does not request a GOV.UK account. The examples show wording and local status messages only. They must not say that a household automation was enabled or an address subscribed.

